[en.C15_DESC]
After the Ultimate Battle, according to the Canterlot Pact, the Crystal Empire was forced to sign an unequal treaty with the newly established Equestria Empire and the Changeling Empire: Princess Cadance and Shining Armor abdicated in favor of Flurry Heart, and because Flurry Heart was too young, the real power of the empire fell into the hooves of the political advisors sent by Empress Cozy Glow. On the other hand, the Canterlot Pact stipulated that the Crystal Empire must unconditionally pay tribute to the Changeling Empire, which made the crystal ponies miserable, and Flurry Heart saw all of this. Now, two years have passed, and Flurry Heart has grown up and begun to seek and unite supporters among the ministers of the empire, gradually forming a political force to counter the political advisors.

But, is it too late for all of this? This ancient empire, which has just awakened, has once again fallen into decline after a brief prosperity, and the political advisors of the Equestria Empire, the agents of the Changeling Empire, the royal supporters, the revolutionaries, the equalists... all these forces are tearing this country apart. However, they are far from the most serious threat to the Crystal Empire...

[en.PIHC_WS_C15_desc]
In the autumn of 1000, the “Big Three” has conquered almost the entire central continent of Equestria. After Tirek returning to his hometown, Cozy Glow and Chrysalis set their sights on the Crystal Empire. But it is obviously a terrible choice to invade a northern frigid country in the fall. In the harsh winter of 1000, the armies of Tirek and Cozy Glow advanced slowly. Under the leadership of Princess Cadance and Shining Armor, the Crystal Empire organized a formidable defense force, and the Crystal Heart provided a powerful magical shield for the Crystal Empire’s army. The war seemed to be in a stalemate, but the resources of the Crystal Empire were slowly drying up, and the front line was shrinking bit by bit.
By the summer of the following year, the harsh winter could no longer protect the Crystal Empire, and the armies of Cozy Glow and Chrysalis launched a summer offensive again. The vanguard forces advanced to the outskirts of the capital, but they still could not break through the powerful magical shield of the Crystal Heart. As summer quickly turned into autumn, winter was not far away. For the Crystal Empire, the harsh winter was both a shelter and a dagger in the back: Cozy Glow and Chrysalis had to break the Crystal Heart before winter, but if the magical shield of the Crystal Heart was broken, the Crystal Empire and the invading army would be swallowed up altogether, by the severe cold of the Windigos. In the end, Cozy Glow and Chrysalis had to back down to the Crystal Empire, and even the once most resolute couple, Princess Cadance and Shining Armor, had to sit down at the negotiating table.
The “Big Three” and the Crystal Empire decided to compromise: Empress Cozy Glow promised the Crystal Empire freedom, but demanded that Princess Cadance and Shining Armor abdicate, the Crystal Empire will be come a nominal vassal of Equestria, be demilitarized, and the government must work with the Equestria Empire; Queen Chrysalis also guaranteed the independence of the Crystal Empire, but demanded that the Crystal Empire pay tribute to the Changelings, to ensure that those who had returned to their original forms would no longer be hungry. The “Crystal Empire Ceasefire” was signed in the autumn of 1001, and shortly after attached to the Canterlot Pact for formal confirmation, and thus everything was settled. The Crystal Ponies knew that an era had ended...

Flurry Heart saw all of this. She was a puppet favored by Empress Cozy Glow - she retained the blood of an alicorn and was easy to control because of her young age. So Empress Cozy Glow made Flurry Heart the new monarch of the Crystal Empire, but by setting up the Crystal Empire Council, she sidelined this baby alicorn. Most of the seats on the Crystal Empire Council were divided between the Equestria Unity Commission and the Changeling Consultants. With the political advisors of the Equestria Unity Commission holding the most seats, they had effectively monopolized the political affairs of the Crystal Empire. Everything was running as Empress Cozy Glow had hoped.

But Empress Cozy Glow underestimated the loyalty of the Crystal Empire’s subjects to the royal family... In just two years, in elections that should have been manipulated, the support rate of the royal cabinet in the council was rising unstoppably, becoming the most influential force. When Empress Cozy Glow began to take this issue seriously, it was too late.
Another variable she had never thought of was Flurry Heart. With such a rich childhood experience, Flurry Heart began to show an amazing maturity early on. And now, although Flurry Heart was just a foal like Empress Cozy Glow, she had already begun to actively participate in the political affairs of the Crystal Empire, and her exposure was increasing... Under her increasingly steady leadership, the support of the royal family was becoming more united.
In the chaotic political environment of the Crystal Empire, ideological consensus is even more difficult to achieve, and the old-Harmonics, Equalists and Democrats are also conducting their activities both openly and secretly. The Crystal Empire is now a crazy stage where every pony has the opportunity to show their political talent...

